    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="5">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Duns">Duns</ref> 5</head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">Gyf Wealh Ænglisne man ofslea, ne ðearf he hine hide[r] ofer buton be healfan were gyldan, ne Ænglisc Wylisne geon ofer ðe ma, sy he ðegenboren, sy he ceorlboren: healf wer ðær ætfealð.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">If a Welshman kills an Englishman [on the other side of the river] he need only pay him over here half of his wergeld; just as an Englishman does not have to pay [more] to a Welshmen [slain] over there. [This is the case] whether he was high- or low-born: half the wergeld falls away.</ab>
        <ab type="supplementaryText" xml:lang="und">Si Waliscus Anglicum occidat, non cogitur eum superreddere nisi dimidio weregildo, nec Anglicus Waliscum, sit de tainis sit de uillanis oriundus: dimidia uuera cadit ibi.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
